-- ProfileRelationship — a connection between two profiles. Two
-- EntityRef<"profile"> fields (`profileAId`, `profileBId`) share the
-- SAME phantom shape; their distinct labels ("Profile A" / "Profile B")
-- live in the TS-side `fieldLabels` block — humanize defaults
-- "Profile A Id" / "Profile B Id" mis-describe the entity-ref fields.
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity (label / description / icon) is
-- registered by defineSystemEntity on the TS side.
--
-- Phase 3c of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3c-profile-relations.md.
-- First entity where two fields share the same EntityRef phantom
-- (both `Id<profile>`). The per-field Labelable instances are keyed
-- `profile_relationship.profileAId` and
-- `profile_relationship.profileBId` so they don't shadow each other —
-- the override mechanism scopes per dotted-path, not per phantom.

@entity
@codeName "profile_relationship"
@label "Profile Relationship"
@description "A connection between two profiles (friend, partner, owner, …)"
@icon "git-merge"
@fieldLabel "profileAId" "Profile A"
@fieldLabel "profileBId" "Profile B"
ProfileRelationship = ProfileRelationship profileAId: EntityRef<"profile"> profileBId: EntityRef<"profile"> type: String note: Maybe String
